I hadn't even *tried* a barbarian since my first ascension around 6
years ago.  this one was basically pretty easy, but what the hell,
I'll post it.

well, maybe it wasn't *that* easy.  I burned through 3 "LS and only
didn't use up the one I was wearing because of two of the three !FH I
found all game (had used the third to boost my HP while in the
dungeon).  never had =regen (though I found a couple rings that I
never ided).  never found a ?geno or /poly (and only !poly was quaffed
by a monster), though I haven't polypiled in my last 6 ascensions.
castle wand of wishing was 0:1.  only one tengu left a corpse, so I
needed a ring to control the teleportitis that corpse gave me.  never
found "refl and didn't have reflection or levitation until Medusa's
level.  dug down, came back up, killed her, and found lev boots and my
shield of reflection in Perseus's statue.  whew.  other than that,
though, nothing too hard.

never found any unholy water and couldn't fountain-dip for any, but I
met a lich, ducked back to the level I'd just been on, pulled out some
uncursed water I'd been saving for just such an encounter, and hung
around him until he cursed me.  the water got it on the first try, so
I beat him down and called it good.  yay for not genociding L.
finally I could curse my numerous scrolls of teleportation and destroy
armour.

my amulet of magical breathing sure came in handy, as it allowed me to
obtain a few resistances from dragons, gain strength from giants, and
dispose of a few troll corpses without choking (or burning any more
"LS, I suppose).  needed a blue dragon to teach me shock resistance--
puddings and gelatinous cubes were very unobliging.  found a ring for
it well after the dragon.

Rodney mostly left me alone, though he found me shortly after I was
all but nekkid to enchant/fooproof some armour or other in the main
dungeon.  I had several turns between finishing that and when he
popped in to get dressed, but I plumb forgot.  d'oh.  touch of death,
there goes "LS #3.  he double-troubled me 2 or 3 times, so the 8 kills
represent fewer meetings.

sacced a werefoo corpse to summon Yeenoghu but didn't get another
human corpse at a convenient time, and I was going for some degree of
speed, so I did have to face Juiblex.  as usual, he engulfed me once
and made me ill, and I got out of it with no problem.

I had all but resigned myself to using an ordinary long sword for the
rest of the game (Cleaver and my staring two-handed sword were out,
seeing as I needed my shield for reflection), but I came across Frosty
in an Orcustown shop.  hmm, come to think of it, I'd also been
planning on getting crowned for Stormy, but I suppose it figures that
the one time I actually want to be crowned, it doesn't happen.

stairs to Vlad's tower were on Baalzebub's level--hadn't seen them in
anything other than an ordinary maze (or maybe a wiztower level)
before.  his throne let me id a couple things.  no other thrones
(except in the castle, above) gave me anything useful and usually
vanished on the first or second sit-down.

astral plane wasn't as easy as usual--I've been finding the right
altar on the first try a lot lately, but this time, it was the second
(Famine), after a trip to, I think, the neutral altar.  Death was on
the scene there, and it was crowded enough that I just made a break
for it both ways, but if his attacks can lower max HP, he must have
hit me, because I was missing about 13 of them when I ended the game.
ah, well.  also needed a !FH shortly after meeting him.  big surprise.

